<article>
    <h1>{$selectedSection}</h1>
    <section>
        <h2>Orientation of co-ordinate system</h2>
        <p>In the XY-plane, we draw the {`\\(x\\)`}-axis pointing to the right and the {`\\(y\\)`}-axis pointing <em>up</em>. This is called <em>right-handed system</em> in the sense that if <strong>we face towards the {`\\(y\\)`}-axis, the {`\\(x\\)`}-axis points to the <em>right</em></strong>. But, this is not the only orientation in use. On computer or mobile screens, the {`\\(y\\)`}-axis points <em>down</em> and the co-ordinate system is no longer right-handed. But in physics and mathematics, we use right-handed co-ordinate systems.</p>
    </section>
    <section>
        <h2>Direction of a plane</h2>
        <p>As we know  the XY-coordinate frame is a plane. In three dimensions, a plane can be drawn in infinitely many ways. Just like we talk about direction of a line, we can talk about direction (or orientation) of a plane. The direction of a plane is defined to be along the perpendicular to the plane.</p>
