        <p>
            The above relation combined with distributivity, we can write the dot product between vectors {`\\(\\vec{a} = a_x\\hat{i} + a_y\\hat{j} + a_z\\hat{k}\\)`} and {`\\(\\vec{b} = b_x\\hat{i} + b_y\\hat{j} + b_z\\hat{k}\\)`} as <span style="display:flex;flex-direction:column;max-width:500px;justify-content:flex-start;margin-top: 1em;margin-left:-2em;">
                {`\\(
                    \\vec{a}\\times\\vec{b} = (a_x\\hat{i} + a_y\\hat{j} + a_z\\hat{k})\\times (b_x\\hat{i} + b_y\\hat{j} + b_z\\hat{k})\\)\\(
                    = (a_yb_z - a_zb_y)\\hat{i} + (a_zb_x - a_xb_z)\\hat{j} + (a_xb_y - a_yb_x)\\hat{k} 
                    \\)
                    \\(
                    = \\begin{vmatrix}
                        a_y & a_z\\\\
                        b_y & b_z\\\\
                      \\end{vmatrix}  \\hat{i}  +
                      \\begin{vmatrix}
                        a_z & a_x\\\\
                        b_z & b_x\\\\
                      \\end{vmatrix}  \\hat{j}  +
                      \\begin{vmatrix}
                        a_x & a_y\\\\
                        b_x & b_y\\\\
                      \\end{vmatrix}  \\hat{k}
                        \\)`}
            </span> 
        </p>
